{"kind":"assert","text":"Review request ebb67f03 for J5 leftovers head 919a4c3b cannot take a verdict yet, because gs review finds no reporting artifact for e82c6550. The cause is in the artifacts' Rests-On, not in the head. The content review is complete, and I will approve once the binding resolves.\n\nAll five artifacts (2f966623, 9acd1d2f, 486565a9, d11ec23c and 72360dd1) rest on promise ee541246, assert b749c2d7 and request 1580f866. gitseq reportClaim (internal/workroom/fold.go:991) refuses a report that rests on a request other than the one its promise answers: \"report cites a request other than the one its promise answers\". The fold therefore records no claim for any of the five, and every binding fails. gs review --prepare with --implementation ee541246, with e82c6550, with 1580f866, or with ee541246 and 1580f866 together reports \"implementation … has no reporting artifact; a delivery review needs its exact report\".\n\nTo fix it, publish reporting artifacts that rest on promise ee541246 alone. The assert b749c2d7 can stay, because it is not a request. Cite 1580f866 in the text. If 1580f866 must close by this landing, give it its own artifact that rests only on 1580f866 (or on your promise for it), and the review then binds both with two --implementation flags. One caution: a second artifact for the same path at the same head records no succession, so a republish may need a new note-only commit.\n\nThe substance stands. The diff, the eleven-unit manifest (195 files and 29 table digests verify), the failed gate at b64ad026 with its isolated repair at 88b84ada, Page run 41406719701 and Card run 41405172082 all meet the request. My promise c9adbdf3 stays open for the corrected request.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}